&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;LaunchDarkly helps engineering teams ship software faster and more safely through feature management, experimentation, and AI delivery tooling. As a GTM AI Engineer, you will design, build, and operate the AI-powered systems that make our sales, marketing, customer success, and partnerships teams more effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will sit at the intersection of engineering and revenue. You’ll turn messy go-to-market workflows into reliable, measurable automation, such as agents that research accounts, tools that surface buying signals, and pipelines that keep our data trustworthy. You’ll work directly with GTM stakeholders to find high-leverage problems, ship quickly, and prove impact with data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build LLM-powered agents and workflows for use cases like account research, lead and account prioritization, outbound personalization, call summarization, deal inspection, renewal risk detection, and customer health insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on end user experience to optimize delivery of content, process adherence and tool utilization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate AI systems with the GTM stack (Salesforce, Outreach, Gong, Marketo, Slack, Zoom, data warehouse, and enrichment providers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain data pipelines that unify product usage, CRM, marketing, and support data into reliable inputs for models and agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Marketing, CS, and RevOps leaders to translate business problems into technical solutions, and prioritize by revenue impact and effort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish evaluation frameworks, guardrails, and monitoring for AI outputs, covering accuracy, hallucination rates, cost, latency, and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use LaunchDarkly’s own products, such as feature flags, AI Configs, and experimentation, to roll out, test, and iterate on GTM AI systems safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype quickly, then productionize the winners with solid engineering practices (testing, observability, documentation, access controls).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable GTM teams through training, documentation, and playbooks so AI tools are adopted and trusted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on the AI tooling landscape and recommend build vs. buy decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of software engineering, data engineering, or ML/AI engineering experience (or equivalent hands-on experience)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Python and/or TypeScript, plus SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building applications with LLMs (prompt design, tool use/function calling, RAG, agent frameworks, structured outputs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating with REST/GraphQL APIs and SaaS platforms, ideally CRM and sales engagement tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data warehouses and transformation tools (Snowflake, BigQuery, dbt, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to evaluate and monitor AI system quality using test sets, human review, and automated evals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, with the ability to explain technical tradeoffs to non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward shipping, iterating, and measuring outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Target pay ranges based on Geographic Zones* for Level 4:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Zone 1: &lt;em&gt;San Francisco/Bay Area or NYC Metropolitan Area, Boston, Seattle&lt;/em&gt; - &lt;em&gt;$196,600&lt;span class=&quot;collapsed-field-text&quot;&gt; - $270,270&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;**&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Zone 2:&lt;em&gt; Irvine, LA, Monterey, Santa Barbara, Santa Rosa, Austin, Portland, Philadelphia, Chicago - $176,900&lt;span class=&quot;collapsed-field-text&quot;&gt; - $243,210&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;**&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;LaunchDarkly operates from a place of high trust and transparency; we are happy to state the pay range for our open roles to best align with your needs. Exact compensation may vary based on skills, experience, and location.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;*Within the United States, our geographic pay zones are defined by counties surrounding major metropolitan areas.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;**Restricted Stock Units (RSUs), health, vision, and dental insurance, and mental health benefits in addition to salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About LaunchDarkly:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modern software delivery was supposed to be the foundation for a thriving digital business but reality has proven otherwise. Slow, inefficient development cycles, costly outages, and fragmented customer experiences are preventing developers from building their best software. The LaunchDarkly platform helps developers innovate on new features faster while protecting them with a safety valve to instantly rewind when things go wrong. Developers can target product experiences to any customer segment and maximize the business impact of every feature. And by gradually rolling out new application components, they escape nightmare &quot;big-bang&quot; technology migrations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The LaunchDarkly platform was built to guide engineers to the next frontier of DevOps by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the velocity and stability of software releases, without the fear of end customer outages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering targeted experiences by easily personalizing features to customer cohorts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximizing the business impact of every feature through the ability to experiment and optimize&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating the release and optimization of software to provide consistent experiences across mobile platforms and device types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the effectiveness and productivity of engineering teams, by providing insights into engineering cadence and stability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At LaunchDarkly, we believe in the power of teams. We&#39;re building a team that is humble, open, collaborative, respectful and kind. We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. LD invites any applicant to review our written Affirmative Action Plan. To do so, contact People Ops at &lt;a class=&quot;notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover&quot; href=&quot;mailto:hr@launchdarkly.com&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;link-annotation-unknown-block-id--893544457&quot;&gt;hr@launchdarkly.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do you need a disability accommodation?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Fill out this&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdYb_7upYMtdRVXzvXGHGfQw0pU2FNma-6Rwp-I6NjKm7SYNw/viewform&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;accommodations request form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and someone from our People Operations team will contact you for assistance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, LaunchDarkly recruiters will only contact you from &lt;a href=&quot;https://launchdarkly.slack.com/team/UKEE4GBS6&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;@LaunchDarkly&lt;/a&gt;.com email addresses or via LinkedIn from &quot;Verified Recruiter&quot; accounts.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Be cautious of emails from other domains.&amp;nbsp; Legitimate LaunchDarkly recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before making a job offer. LaunchDarkly will never make a job offer without conducting a formal interview process. Our interview process does not involve asking detailed questions by email. If you are ever unsure about a communication that you receive, don&#39;t click any links—visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://launchdarkly.com/careers/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Careers | LaunchDarkly&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; directly for confirmed job openings and links to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please notify us of any fraudulent representation by sending an email to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:careers@launchdarkly.com&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;careers@launchdarkly.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Discord has a highly engaged community of millions of daily active users who use the platform for many different reasons, but there’s one thing that nearly everyone does: &lt;strong&gt;play video games.&lt;/strong&gt; Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming, and we are focused on making it easier and more fun for people to hang out before, during, and after playing games.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Discord&#39;s Enterprise Technology org is building a software engineering discipline from the ground up, and this is one of its first engineering hires. The Enterprise Platform team is brand new. You will not be inheriting a mature system or a long backlog: you will own core domains of the platform that turns the internal systems enabling Discordians into self-service software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Discord&#39;s mission is to cultivate belonging, and doing that at scale requires internal systems that move as fast as the product itself. The mission of this role is to turn our enterprise infrastructure into self-service software. Your job is to replace manual consoles and tickets with a platform of reusable primitives, building blocks like &quot;provision a device&quot; or &quot;push an IAM policy or app integration through code,&quot; exposed through clean APIs and self-service portals. As a code-forward Senior engineer, you will design abstractions that hide the messy reality of Okta, Jamf, and Terraform (our identity, device management, and infrastructure-as-code tools) behind interfaces people actually want to use, operating with a platform-as-a-product mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the device fleet as code: Move device configuration off consoles and into versioned, API-driven infrastructure for endpoint management and hardware provisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate the identity layer: Manage identity systems and their connections to downstream apps as code, from SSO and SCIM integrations to account workflows, so changes ship through version control and CI/CD instead of an admin console.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own app delivery and Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC): Build deployment pipelines and provisioning patterns that let internal systems be built and changed safely, establishing CI/CD standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the self-service layer: Design and ship the APIs, CLIs, and portals that compose primitives into paved paths, like a new hire&#39;s first day, where software access and group memberships land in one automated, auditable flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your domain end to end: Take core components of the platform from design through production with no code boundaries, writing the RFCs and documentation for the areas you own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Should Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years building and operating production software and systems at a technology company, with a track record of owning projects end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering fundamentals. You write production code (we lean on Go, Python, and TypeScript), and design, test, and ship it. This is not a systems admin role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on IAM experience (SSO, SCIM, OAuth/OIDC, RBAC) and working fluency with infrastructure as code (Terraform) and CI/CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience treating endpoint or infrastructure configuration as an API-driven engineering surface rather than console work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A platform-as-a-product mindset. You care whether people actually adopt what you build, not just whether it ships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort owning complex, multi-milestone projects through ambiguity, and energy for building in a greenfield environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Okta, Jamf, or Intune.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with identity and access governance for non-human, workload, or AI-agent principals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background at a high-growth consumer tech company with a highly technical employee base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. This position will also be eligible for equity and benefits. Benefits include medical, dental, and vision insurance; a 401(k) plan; life and disability insurance; paid time off; and paid parental leave. Our salary ranges are determined by role and level. Within the range, individual pay is determined by additional factors, including job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Please note that the compensation details listed in role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include equity, or benefits. Applications for this role are accepted on an ongoing basis.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$196,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$245,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Discord?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming. We&#39;re a multiplatform, multigenerational and multiplayer platform that helps people deepen their friendships around games and shared interests, and helps developers build and grow their businesses. We believe games give us a way to have fun with our favorite people, whether listening to music together or grinding in competitive matches for diamond rank. &lt;strong&gt;Join us in our mission! Your future is just a click away!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discord is committed to inclusion and providing reasonable accommodations during the interview process. &lt;/strong&gt;We want you to feel set up for success, so if you are in need of reasonable accommodations, please let your recruiter know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please see our Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy for details regarding Discord’s collection and usage of personal information relating to the application and recruitment process by clicking&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://discord.com/terms/applicant-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;HERE.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? &lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; is building the future of finance for people, institutions and their agents, with one place to trade crypto, equities, derivatives and prediction markets, use stablecoins, and connect AI agents with clear controls. The bar is high and the pace is intense, and we like it that way. This isn’t a place for complacency. It’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits and do the best work of your career. If you’re ready to build the future of finance with a championship team who refuse to settle for “good enough,” you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for in-person working sessions&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Senior Software Engineer, Native Mobile to join the App Infra team within the&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers/product-groups&quot;&gt; Consumer &amp;amp; Business&lt;/a&gt; group. This team is executing a greenfield rewrite of Coinbase&#39;s retail mobile app from React Native to native Swift and Kotlin, using AI-assisted code generation to deliver a dramatically faster, higher-quality experience for millions of customers. You&#39;ll bring deep iOS or Android expertise to build core app surfaces, contribute to the design of Coinbase’s native mobile agentic workflow, and contribute to the foundation of Coinbase’s future mobile platform as product teams onboard to the native codebase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate every other Frontend engineer at Coinbase by defining architectural patterns, improving build speeds, and defining optimal development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the development of core app surfaces in Swift and Kotlin, translating existing React Native flows into performant native implementations that meet strict performance budgets, and setting the project-level quality bar through code and design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build within the AI-assisted code generation loop, orchestrating AI as a force multiplier by leveraging LLM-driven translation while applying native mobile expertise to validate architecture, catch edge cases, and ensure production-quality outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product teams during onboarding to review native PRs, challenge suboptimal patterns, and attack slow paths the team has accepted, such as flaky tests, painful deploys, or ambiguous handoffs between native and React Native codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive performance optimization across device tiers, architecting robust solutions through trade-off analysis to eliminate loading indicators, scroll jank, and stall counts, with particular attention to low-end Android devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the dual-app parity strategy during the transition period, identifying and killing technical debt that matters while ensuring feature and bug fix synchronization between codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of iOS or Android mobile software engineering experience (Swift/iOS or Kotlin/Android).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build and ship performant mobile applications with a focus on frame stability, cold start optimization, and responsive UI across diverse device populations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Swift or Kotlin with working knowledge of the other, and willingness to develop cross-platform fluency, as engineers on this team own both iOS and Android.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile CI/CD pipelines, build systems, and release processes, with a track record of delivering project-level outcomes that compound beyond the immediate cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and measurable gains in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Job# P79161&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Base salary varies by location (see range below). Total compensation may also include equity and bonus eligibility, and benefits (medical, dental, vision, 401(k)).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual base salary range (excluding equity and bonus):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$186,065&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$218,900 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Application Limit: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Candidates may submit a maximum of 3 applications within a 6-month period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer: &lt;/strong&gt;Coinbase is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. Applicants with criminal histories will be considered consistent with applicable federal, state, and local laws.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Applicants: &lt;/strong&gt;View&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/WHD/legacy/files/eppac.pdf&quot;&gt; Employee Rights&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt; Know Your Rights&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://static-assets.coinbase.com/e-verify.pdf&quot;&gt; E-Verify&lt;/a&gt; Notice of Participation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations: &lt;/strong&gt;If you are an individual with a disability who needs a reasonable accommodation, email us your request and contact info at accommodations[at]coinbase.com.&amp;nbsp;Need screen reading technology?&lt;a href=&quot;https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/screen-reader/kgejglhpjiefppelpmljglcjbhoiplfn&quot;&gt; Click here&lt;/a&gt; to download a free compatible screen reader and view the&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.chromevox.com/tutorial/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;tutorial&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy &amp;amp; Arbitration: &lt;/strong&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/legal/applicant_privacy_notice&quot;&gt; Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. US applicants: By submitting your application, you agree to&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/legal/application-arbitration-agreement&quot;&gt; Arbitration of Disputes&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
